Summary
-------
Developed and integrated a new dark matter close-encounter analysis
module into the MW–M31 merger simulation pipeline. The work focused on
building the theoretical framework, numerical architecture, encounter
search algorithms, diagnostic systems, and visualization infrastructure
for tracking gravitational close encounters between collisionless
dark matter particles in an N-body simulation environment.

NOTE:
This work session focused on implementation and integration.
The full section has not yet been executed end-to-end on simulation data,
so runtime validation, debugging under production loads, and physical
verification of outputs remain pending.

